{
  "$comment": [
    "U7: thermal vias (R11) and fiducials (R12).",
    "",
    "U2 (W25Q512JV, WSON-8) had 0 vias in its 4.65 x 5.20 mm thermal pad and needs",
    "9; U4 (CH224K, ESSOP-10) had 0 in its 3.30 x 2.10 mm pad and needs 5. Both",
    "pads are on /GND, and both were reachable only after checking every layer:",
    "U2's pad has QSPI_IO2 and QSPI_IO1 running under it on the bottom (put there",
    "by U6) and MOSI_R_MCU crossing Inner1 corner to corner, so a plain 3x3 grid",
    "would short three vias. Positions come from a clearance-aware grid search",
    "(scratch place_thermal.py) against all four layers, then greedy max-spread.",
    "",
    "All 14 are 0.6/0.3 -- 0.15 mm annular ring, which is JLC's minimum. The 0.45",
    "via that would also have fitted U4 leaves 0.075 mm and was rejected. All are",
    "TENTED both sides: an untented via in a thermal pad wicks solder during",
    "reflow and leaves a void under the pad, which is the half of TV-001 that is",
    "easy to miss.",
    "",
    "Fiducials: 3 on F.Cu for 122 SMD components, placed at the clearest points",
    "found by scanning the top layer -- west-north (r=2.33 mm of bare space),",
    "centre-south (4.51) and east-south (9.13). The triangle is deliberately",
    "asymmetric so a vision system can tell a 180-degree flip. They are marked",
    "board_only so 'Update PCB from Schematic' will not delete parts that have no",
    "symbol, and excluded from BOM and CPL."
  ],
